erfacing with new  people has its benefits as well  you know if you're too insular there are  problems like genetic bottlenecks you  may exhaust the resources in your in  your  in your territory whereas on the other  end  if you're more open to outside people it  allows you greater genetic diversity  it allows you to acquire technologies  and and resources that you might not  be able to acquire if you just wanted to  stay put with your with your own kind  so you know when we look at kind of the  core values of  of of people on the left or right  we can see those dynamics at play you  know people on the left tend to be more  open to other cultures  they tend to embrace other cultures they  tend to be more  sexually open because you know  that would be helpful to you if you're  if you're migrating to a new tribe of  people  and would allow you to interface with  them interbreed with them it would allow  you to acquire certain kinds of  immunities  that they had to local pathogens by  interfacing  and and having offering with them uh but  there's a certain advantage to staying  put  so these are some very core um  underlying psychologies behind our  political orientations  and they may have served an old purpose  you

